{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229176-e2-was-the-gem-of-immortality-an-innovation-of-the-last-years-of-the-high-fa","id":1229176,"title":"E2 - Was the Gem of Immortality an innovation of the last years of the High FA?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-21T10:29:35-07:00","id":1229176,"title":"E2 - Was the Gem of Immortality an innovation of the last years of the High FA?","content":"Much of the setting of the Lands of Creation book feels like it revolves around the Exalted being still mortal and racing against a clock. I can hand wave Peaches of Immortality having the effects that they do by their effects being the result of a Working, but what about the Gem of Immortality? Were they a discovery of the final days of the Solar Deliberative?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T11:18:20-07:00","id":1229183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229176-e2-was-the-gem-of-immortality-an-innovation-of-the-last-years-of-the-high-fa#post1229176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can hand wave Peaches of Immortality having the effects that they do by their effects being the result of a Working...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but why do that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229176-e2-was-the-gem-of-immortality-an-innovation-of-the-last-years-of-the-high-fa#post1229176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...but what about the Gem of Immortality? Were they a discovery of the final days of the Solar Deliberative?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, and bear with me here, maybe the Exalt (not necessarily a Solar, mind) who discovered immortality didn't deign to share the details with her peers?<br /> <br /> Or perhaps they <i>did </i>know about it, but making them took a bit more than the rules presently call for; perhaps a manse that generates a Gem of Immortality <i>has</i> to have the Maintenance flaw, in the form of having to be watered with Solar blood every fifty years to stay working, and thus possessing one was a tad suspect?<br /> <br /> \u200bOr maybe the Solars knew it existed, but there could only be one of them at a time, and none of the characters we see are the one who has it?<br /> <br /> Or perhaps the Solars of the time didn't trust their immortality to a mere stone that they'd have to keep on their person/socketed into one of their artifacts at all times?<br /> <br /> \u200bOr maybe it's just a sign that the Gem of Immortality shouldn't have been written into the setting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-21-2018, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T12:34:26-07:00","id":1229195,"title":"","content":"All good ideas, but I like the idea of relatively easily manufactured Immortality for all DBs who pledge themselves to your Solar. You have to start your new Gentes somehow. Perhaps the Manse was one of those special creations that required truly unique components to create, such as those Essence Pearls that you need a mortal to commit their entire Essence pool into an oyster created with Craft Genesis and the only way to create new ones is by finding a surviving colony of those oysters and have a mortal permanently sacrifice his or her ability to channel essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 06-23-2018, 01:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T13:36:30-07:00","id":1229215,"title":"","content":"I see that gem as a bit of a difficult priority to stick to. It's a high level hearthstone that won't do the owner any good until they reach advanced age. So why get one early, when other hearthstones of comparable power are more likely to help you reach that advanced age at all? And then, when you are at that age...then you may not want to lose any of the stones you have to rebuild a manse to make a gem of immortality, or maybe you just have nowhere to do it.<br /> <br /> The stone exists, sure, but it's hardly the only powerful hearthstone worth chasing, so not everyone will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T21:49:11-07:00","id":1229293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BjornTheFellhanded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229176-e2-was-the-gem-of-immortality-an-innovation-of-the-last-years-of-the-high-fa?p=1229215#post1229215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see that gem as a bit of a difficult priority to stick to. It's a high level hearthstone that won't do the owner any good until they reach advanced age. So why get one early, when other hearthstones of comparable power are more likely to help you reach that advanced age at all? And then, when you are at that age...then you may not want to lose any of the stones you have to rebuild a manse to make a gem of immortality, or maybe you just have nowhere to do it.<br /> <br /> The stone exists, sure, but it's hardly the only powerful hearthstone worth chasing, so not everyone will.</div> </div> </div> </div>The stone isn\u2019t for Celestials, they still have Peaches of Immortality which they can secure access to reliably. The Stone is there for DBs, or maybe Dragon Kings and Jade Folk Artisans. People who are valuable, possibly leaders, and you want to win to your side and then keep them around forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 06-23-2018, 01:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T21:58:58-07:00","id":1229294,"title":"","content":"I would imagine that the stone was engineered for far more often during the Shogunate than during the High First Age, for the reasons you mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T22:44:58-07:00","id":1229305,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s a good idea, but you\u2019d have to tell people playing mid-First Age games that the Stone of Immortality is off the table as a Hearthstone choice, and that never flies.<br /> <br /> (See also: \u201cThe Solar Charm set has reached its utter peak of efficiency through years of new Charm development throughout the First Age\u201d getting effectively retconned as soon as people realized it meant Primordial War game Solars would need a shittier set.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","user":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","date":". 06-22-2018, 01:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T03:19:04-07:00","id":1229333,"title":"","content":"This is the great thing about Wild-Born hearthstones in 3e. You can take any effect you want and not break the game by making it one-of-a-kind and totally unreproducible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T06:38:21-07:00","id":1229357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229176-e2-was-the-gem-of-immortality-an-innovation-of-the-last-years-of-the-high-fa?p=1229293#post1229293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The stone isn\u2019t for Celestials, they still have Peaches or Immortality which they can secure access to reliably. The Stone is there for DBs, or maybe Dragon Kings and Jade Folk Artisans. People who are valuable, possibly leaders, and you want to win to your side and then keep them around forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the effort it would take to produce even a single stone (no, it wouldn't be trivial even for the more powerful Solars) there would always be way too many people you might want to give it to than you'd have stones. Which means, you'd have to make choices.Choices that would also have negative consequences, because you'd be forced to pass some important supporters in favour of others, thust creating seeds of strife and discontentment. Besides, with a heavily limited supply you might end up giving the stone to someone else. Say, a lover. Or a halfcaste child. Or keep it for yourself just in case.<br /> <br /> Basically, it's the whole assumption of an existence of &quot;relatively easily manufactured Immortality&quot; that is faulty here. There's nothing even remotely suggesting that it would be easy, or even &quot;relatively easy&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":434,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","user":"Astralporing","date":". 06-22-2018, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T03:06:27-07:00","id":1229554,"title":"","content":"Indeed, a manse-rating-of-five, earth-aspected hearthstone is not &quot;relatively easily manufactured&quot; by any metric.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T07:06:26-07:00","id":1229588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229176-e2-was-the-gem-of-immortality-an-innovation-of-the-last-years-of-the-high-fa?p=1229554#post1229554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, a manse-rating-of-five, earth-aspected hearthstone is not &amp;quot;relatively easily manufactured&amp;quot; by any metric.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may be overstating the ease by which a Solar could Wyld Shape a Demesne and then Wyld Shape the materials and workers to build the Manse after you design it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T17:15:22-07:00","id":1229678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229176-e2-was-the-gem-of-immortality-an-innovation-of-the-last-years-of-the-high-fa?p=1229588#post1229588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may be overstating the ease by which a Solar could Wyld Shape a Demesne and then Wyld Shape the materials and workers to build the Manse after you design it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which might be what most Solars did back in the FA. Which means those Manses and Hearthstones were destroyed as the area was reclaimed into the Wyld.<br /> <br /> So maybe there were several thousands of them back then, but the population was in the billions.<br /> <br /> Also, there is nothing that says the knowledge of how one is made survived both the Usurpation and the Great Contagion. There might have been both Lunars and Sidereals that knew how to build that kind of Manse, but they might not have survived or shared their knowledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-24T07:29:13-07:00","id":1229798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229176-e2-was-the-gem-of-immortality-an-innovation-of-the-last-years-of-the-high-fa?p=1229305#post1229305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(See also: \u201cThe Solar Charm set has reached its utter peak of efficiency through years of new Charm development throughout the First Age\u201d getting effectively retconned as soon as people realized it meant Primordial War game Solars would need a shittier set.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That would have been hilarious, though! Immunity to Some Things Technique. Two Shadows Evasion. Hill-Crossing Leap Technique. Ready in Three Directions Stance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-24T11:13:50-07:00","id":1229832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229176-e2-was-the-gem-of-immortality-an-innovation-of-the-last-years-of-the-high-fa?p=1229798#post1229798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would have been hilarious, though! Immunity to Some Things Technique. Two Shadows Evasion. Hill-Crossing Leap Technique. Ready in Three Directions Stance.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I had all the time in the world, and were more mechanically inclined, &quot;Shittier sets for all the Exalt types for First Age games&quot; is one of those jokes that works the best if you follow through with it to its absurd, overwrought conclusion. Alas, I do not have all the time in the world, and am not particularly mechanically inclined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-24T18:47:18-07:00","id":1229914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229176-e2-was-the-gem-of-immortality-an-innovation-of-the-last-years-of-the-high-fa?p=1229832#post1229832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I had all the time in the world, and were more mechanically inclined, &quot;Shittier sets for all the Exalt types for First Age games&quot; is one of those jokes that works the best if you follow through with it to its absurd, overwrought conclusion. Alas, I do not have all the time in the world, and am not particularly mechanically inclined.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, serif\">Horses Almost Never Fly Approach</span></span><br /> <b>Cost: </b>1m; <b>Mins: </b>Ride 5, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One turn<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Coursing Firebolt Sparkle<br /> The Solar whispers in her mount's ear, convincing it that the impossible has been known to happen. When she attempts to ride over water, clouds, an open gap above a chasm, or similar, she rolls (her mount's current temporary Willpower). As long as it receives one success, she is able to complete the movement; on a failed roll, both her and her mount fall, and her mount loses a point of Willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T08:36:47-07:00","id":1230022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229176-e2-was-the-gem-of-immortality-an-innovation-of-the-last-years-of-the-high-fa?p=1229914#post1229914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, serif\">Horses Almost Never Fly Approach</span></span><br /> <b>Cost: </b>1m; <b>Mins: </b>Ride 5, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One turn<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Coursing Firebolt Sparkle<br /> The Solar whispers in her mount's ear, convincing it that the impossible has been known to happen. When she attempts to ride over water, clouds, an open gap above a chasm, or similar, she rolls (her mount's current temporary Willpower). As long as it receives one success, she is able to complete the movement; on a failed roll, both her and her mount fall, and her mount loses a point of Willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, no, what have you done?! Since you're the Ex3 developer, this charm is now canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T09:32:24-07:00","id":1230030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229176-e2-was-the-gem-of-immortality-an-innovation-of-the-last-years-of-the-high-fa?p=1229832#post1229832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I had all the time in the world, and were more mechanically inclined, &quot;Shittier sets for all the Exalt types for First Age games&quot; is one of those jokes that works the best if you follow through with it to its absurd, overwrought conclusion. Alas, I do not have all the time in the world, and am not particularly mechanically inclined.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shouldn't the current charmset be shittier by that metric, since (outside fo past life memories) the progress the exalted made in the first age has been largely forgotten.<br /> <br /> That said I think &quot;progress&quot; is better expressed through advanced artifacts or the like, not better innate powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T09:37:32-07:00","id":1230032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229176-e2-was-the-gem-of-immortality-an-innovation-of-the-last-years-of-the-high-fa?p=1230030#post1230030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shouldn't the current charmset be shittier by that metric, since (outside fo past life memories) the progress the exalted made in the first age has been largely forgotten.<br /> <br /> That said I think &quot;progress&quot; is better expressed through advanced artifacts or the like, not better innate powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>The First Edition corebook, in the sidebar on custom Charms, said &quot;No you can't just make a custom version of an existing Charm with a lower mote cost; the Charms currently in use by the Exalted were honed to the absolute limit of efficiency over the millennia of the First Age; if you want to make a custom Charm, it has to be meaningfully different from an existing Charm.&quot; Or some such. And it's obviously just something being said to discourage &quot;I want to remake Excellent Strike but cheaper,&quot; but it also established that the Exalted of the early First Age must have had shittier Charmsets.<br /> <br /> Presumably the increased efficiency of modern Charms are transmitted through the memories of the Exaltation.<br /> <br /> (Then we wrote Dreams of the First Age and wanted to present the whole scope of First Age history as playable, at which point... no. Out that concept went!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T22:34:05-07:00","id":1230199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229176-e2-was-the-gem-of-immortality-an-innovation-of-the-last-years-of-the-high-fa?p=1230032#post1230032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The First Edition corebook, in the sidebar on custom Charms, said &quot;No you can't just make a custom version of an existing Charm with a lower mote cost; the Charms currently in use by the Exalted were honed to the absolute limit of efficiency over the millennia of the First Age; if you want to make a custom Charm, it has to be meaningfully different from an existing Charm.&quot; Or some such. And it's obviously just something being said to discourage &quot;I want to remake Excellent Strike but cheaper,&quot; but it also established that the Exalted of the early First Age must have had shittier Charmsets.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, it isn't like Geoff knew what he was midwifing when the 1e core was being written.<br /> <br /> I think back then there was less concept of the Charmset being native, techniques that were fundamentally inherent to your Exaltation and expressions of that power. They were more clearly widgets, things you learned how to do like shooting a three-pointer or popping a wheelie or doing a kickflip, which meant that presumably you could get &quot;better&quot; at them with practice; you'd train and train and train with Excellent Strike a thousand times a day and eventually be able to execute it with less effort (motes) than someone who just learned it.<br /> <br /> So establishing &quot;yeah, you're not the first person to have this idea; the Solars ruled as god-kings for centuries and have already optimized their magic as best they can, and you've inherited their learnings&quot; wasn't a bad idea in that context.<br /> <br /> Later on, the notion that the native Charmsets were more akin to &quot;this is <i>part </i>of being an Exalt&quot; rather than &quot;this is a thing an Exalt <i>can do</i>&quot; took hold, especially after the Sidereals got their closed Charmset that is intimately tied to their natures as the Chosen of the Maidens. Under that mindset, you can just say &quot;your native Charmset is as good as it gets; it is an integral part of you, your inherent magic. Any specific Charm can't really get 'better' on its own.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T14:23:38-07:00","id":1230641,"title":"","content":"It was either said about the Scarlet Empress or First Age Solars, but a developer once floated the point that for somebody that is anxious about their mortality, a hearthstone isn't entirely a relief from that, because of the need to maintain proximity to the stone and maintenance of the manse, and how those things can be lost, stolen or destroyed.<br /> <br /> (Watch this space for my possibly extensive rant for how weak immortality feels as a motivating factor for people that already live incomprehensibly long amounts of time)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T14:44:45-07:00","id":1230647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229176-e2-was-the-gem-of-immortality-an-innovation-of-the-last-years-of-the-high-fa?p=1230641#post1230641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was either said about the Scarlet Empress or First Age Solars, but a developer once floated the point that for somebody that is anxious about their mortality, a hearthstone isn't entirely a relief from that, because of the need to maintain proximity to the stone and maintenance of the manse, and how those things can be lost, stolen or destroyed.<br /> <br /> (Watch this space for my possibly extensive rant for how weak immortality feels as a motivating factor for people that already live incomprehensibly long amounts of time)</div> </div> </div> </div>Point. I mean, it's been roughly 5k years or so since the Primordial War, yes? Discounting anagathics and premature death (in other words, in a thoroughly hypothetical scenario) that's two or so generations of Solars, and one of Sidereals. IMO, by far the best and most interesting use of immortality macguffins is as something a celestial exalt goes on a quest or mission for for the sake of someone else - a mortal lover, a beloved lieutenant, a Terrestrial friend, a Circlemate cursed by an Abyssal/Deathlord/whatever to age at an increased rate and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T15:20:07-07:00","id":1230655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BjornTheFellhanded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229176-e2-was-the-gem-of-immortality-an-innovation-of-the-last-years-of-the-high-fa?p=1229215#post1229215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see that gem as a bit of a difficult priority to stick to. It's a high level hearthstone that won't do the owner any good until they reach advanced age. So why get one early, when other hearthstones of comparable power are more likely to help you reach that advanced age at all? And then, when you are at that age...then you may not want to lose any of the stones you have to rebuild a manse to make a gem of immortality, or maybe you just have nowhere to do it.<br /> <br /> The stone exists, sure, but it's hardly the only powerful hearthstone worth chasing, so not everyone will.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I\u2019m designing my magical cooking pot to have the power to produce Age-Staving Cordials from common materials at a rate of one-per-week.<br /> <br /> Sure, you could theoretically produce enough anagathic to prolong someone\u2019s life 25% for next to nothing in material costs...<br /> <br /> But that means you can\u2019t use the pot to produce anything else, and it can produce medicines and ointments of much more immediate power. <br /> <br /> (All concoctions lose potency shortly after being poured from the pot, unless you commit motes to keep the dose\u2019s freshness sealed. This caps your ability to stockpile cheaply-produced magical medicines.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T15:58:46-07:00","id":1230668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229176-e2-was-the-gem-of-immortality-an-innovation-of-the-last-years-of-the-high-fa?p=1230647#post1230647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Point. I mean, it's been roughly 5k years or so since the Primordial War, yes? Discounting anagathics and premature death (in other words, in a thoroughly hypothetical scenario) that's two or so generations of Solars, and one of Sidereals. IMO, by far the best and most interesting use of immortality macguffins is as something a celestial exalt goes on a quest or mission for for the sake of someone else - a mortal lover, a beloved lieutenant, a Terrestrial friend, a Circlemate cursed by an Abyssal/Deathlord/whatever to age at an increased rate and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. That's the kind of thing in which it sounds like it could be more fun, because the stakes can feel more immediate, and it's a bit more plausible for the effects to be seen in the course of an actual story. Certainly, it's a thing that figures into narrative surrounding a number of gods and the like.<br /> <br /> It feels to me as though when you're somebody who can naturally live to be around 3,000 years old, actually becoming capable of living indefinitely (or extending it to something even more ridiculously incomprehensible, like 50,000 years) is the kind of thing where it would take ages for it to even stand out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T15:38:14-07:00","id":1230933,"title":"","content":"There's already an artifact in 3e that lets you live forever with minimal effort, anyway. (Well, minimal effort once you <i>have</i> it.) Since it produces Peaches of Immortality, even having it stolen doesn't mean much because you have your entire natural lifespan to get it back or find something to replace it with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T18:53:42-07:00","id":1230973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229176-e2-was-the-gem-of-immortality-an-innovation-of-the-last-years-of-the-high-fa?p=1230933#post1230933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's already an artifact in 3e that lets you live forever with minimal effort, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyway what? Was anybody arguing that there wasn't? This feels like a bit of a non-sequitur.<br /> <br /> Besides, you need to be Essence 5 and resonant with starmetal before Gnomon will make peaches of immortality for you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since it produces Peaches of Immortality, even having it stolen doesn't mean much because you have your entire natural lifespan to get it back or find something to replace it with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of, can somebody remind me if the gem of immortality is described in a manner suggesting that your aging freezes in a manner, or that you just don't feel your years. Say a Dragon Blood has had one since they were twenty, and has lived to a thousand before it is rendered moot; are we assuming that they resume aging towards their three hundred years from the day that the gem was acquired, or do they drop dead immediately?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}